In `check_update`, each reported condition is one of the explicit `if`/`elif` tests in the function body. The test file creates several `CallbackQueryHandler` instances with different `pattern`/`game_pattern` settings and calls `check_update` with updates covering: a non-`Update` object, callback queries with string data that match and do not match regexes, non-string data, missing data plus matching/non-matching `game_short_name`, no patterns at all, a type pattern, a callable pattern, and cases where only one of `pattern` or `game_pattern` is configured. Reading those inputs against the function logic shows that every evaluated condition listed below is reached in at least one case, and each of them evaluates both ways across the full test.

